            <div xml:id="d149">

                <pb facs="0245" n="145" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg145"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00/23733: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Frontera</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Blohm</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Frontera</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-04-26T14:00:00-06:57"><hi rendition="#italic">April 26,
                                1920—2 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received April 27—6:30
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Department’s April 23rd 5 p.m.<anchor n="8" xml:id="d149-f1"/> American citizens
                    and American interests asking me protection against disorganized ruthless bands
                    revolutionists threatening Frontera. Interruption communications expected every
                    moment. Warship draft of 10 feet needed entering river.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Blohm</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
